<phyphox version="1.7" locale="en" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
    <title>Analog Input</title>
    <category>Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense</category>
    <description>Plots the voltage inferred from the analog inputs of the Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense. The mV view uses a nominal 3.3 V, 10-bit conversion and the raw ADC counts remain available.</description>
    <link label="Find more">https://vulgarisation.fr/?lang=en</link>
    <icon format="base64"></icon> 
	<color>009297</color> 
    <translations>
        <translation locale="fr">
            <title>Entrée analogique</title>
            <category>Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense</category>
            <description>Trace la tension déduite des entrées analogiques du Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense. La vue en mV utilise une conversion nominale 3,3 V / 10 bits et les comptes ADC bruts restent disponibles.</description>
            <link label="Plus d'infos">https://vulgarisation.fr/</link>
            <string original="Voltage at A0">Tension mesurée en A0</string>
            <string original="Voltage at A1">Tension mesurée en A1</string>
            <string original="Voltage at A2">Tension mesurée en A2</string>
            <string original="time">temps</string>
            <string original="Analog Input A0">Valeur de l'entrée A0</string>
            <string original="Analog Input A1">Valeur de l'entrée A1</string>
            <string original="Analog Input A2">Valeur de l'entrée A2</string>
            <string original="Voltage">Tension</string>
            <string original="Simple">Simple</string>
            <string original="Raw Data">Raw Data</string>
        <string original="Calibration">Étalonnage</string>
<string original="Gain A0">Facteur A0</string>
<string original="Offset A0">Décalage A0</string>
<string original="Gain A1">Facteur A1</string>
<string original="Offset A1">Décalage A1</string>
<string original="Gain A2">Facteur A2</string>
<string original="Offset A2">Décalage A2</string>
<string original="Setup">Montage</string>
<string original="Use a common ground, short leads and inputs within 0–3.3 V; do not connect mains or negative voltages. Check the terminal voltage with a calibrated meter at two or more levels. Fit U=kq+c for each input, recording source resistance and meter loading. The default 3300/1023 mV/count is a nominal endpoint scale, not a measured ADC reference. High source impedance, sequential channel acquisition and RC loading can alter the result. Use slow signals or an appropriate anti-alias filter.">Utiliser une masse commune, des fils courts et des entrées entre 0 et 3,3 V ; ne pas connecter le secteur ni de tensions négatives. Vérifier la tension aux bornes à au moins deux niveaux avec un instrument étalonné. Ajuster U=kq+c pour chaque entrée en relevant résistance de source et charge de mesure. La valeur 3300/1023 mV/compte est une échelle nominale aux extrémités, sans mesure de la référence ADC. Impédance élevée, acquisition séquentielle et charge RC modifient le résultat. Utiliser des signaux lents ou un filtre anti-repliement adapté.</string>
<string original="Record a stable reference before and after each trial. The BLE interval is at least 50 ms; unavailable sensor readings remain NaN. Fast signals need an independently verified bandwidth and anti-alias filtering.">Enregistrer une référence stable avant et après chaque essai. L’intervalle BLE est d’au moins 50 ms ; les mesures indisponibles restent NaN. Les signaux rapides nécessitent une bande passante vérifiée et un filtre anti-repliement.</string>
<string original="Enter coefficients measured on this apparatus. Defaults are nominal, not a calibration. Changing a coefficient recalculates the entire trace; original readings and settings are exported separately. Clearing data restores the defaults.">Saisir les coefficients mesurés sur ce montage. Les valeurs initiales sont nominales, sans étalonnage. Un changement recalcule toute la courbe ; mesures originales et réglages sont exportés séparément. Effacer les données rétablit les valeurs initiales.</string>
        </translation>
        <translation locale="de">
            <title>Analogeingänge</title>
            <category>Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense</category>
            <description>Die aus den Analogeingängen des Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense abgeleitete Spannung messen. Die mV-Ansicht nutzt eine nominale 3,3-V-Umrechnung für einen 10-Bit-ADC, und die rohen ADC-Zählwerte bleiben verfügbar.</description>
            <link label="Weitere Informationen (englisch)">https://vulgarisation.fr/?lang=en</link>
            <string original="Voltage at A0">Spannung an A0</string>
            <string original="Voltage at A1">Spannung an A1</string>
            <string original="Voltage at A2">Spannung an A2</string>
            <string original="time">Zeit</string>
            <string original="Analog Input A0">Analogeingang A0</string>
            <string original="Analog Input A1">Analogeingang A1</string>
            <string original="Analog Input A2">Analogeingang A2</string>
            <string original="Voltage">Spannung</string>
            <string original="Simple">Einfach</string>
            <string original="Raw Data">Rohdaten</string>
        <string original="Calibration">Kalibrierung</string>
<string original="Gain A0">Faktor A0</string>
<string original="Offset A0">Offset A0</string>
<string original="Gain A1">Faktor A1</string>
<string original="Offset A1">Offset A1</string>
<string original="Gain A2">Faktor A2</string>
<string original="Offset A2">Offset A2</string>
<string original="Setup">Aufbau</string>
<string original="Use a common ground, short leads and inputs within 0–3.3 V; do not connect mains or negative voltages. Check the terminal voltage with a calibrated meter at two or more levels. Fit U=kq+c for each input, recording source resistance and meter loading. The default 3300/1023 mV/count is a nominal endpoint scale, not a measured ADC reference. High source impedance, sequential channel acquisition and RC loading can alter the result. Use slow signals or an appropriate anti-alias filter.">Gemeinsame Masse, kurze Leitungen und Eingänge innerhalb 0–3,3 V verwenden; keine Netzspannung oder negativen Spannungen anschließen. Klemmenspannung an mindestens zwei Pegeln mit kalibriertem Messgerät prüfen. Für jeden Eingang U=kq+c anpassen; Quellwiderstand und Messgerätebelastung erfassen. 3300/1023 mV/Zählwert ist eine nominale Endpunktskala, keine gemessene ADC-Referenz. Hoher Quellwiderstand, sequenzielle Abtastung und RC-Belastung beeinflussen das Ergebnis. Langsame Signale oder geeignete Anti-Aliasing-Filter verwenden.</string>
<string original="Record a stable reference before and after each trial. The BLE interval is at least 50 ms; unavailable sensor readings remain NaN. Fast signals need an independently verified bandwidth and anti-alias filtering.">Vor und nach jedem Versuch eine stabile Referenz aufzeichnen. Das BLE-Intervall beträgt mindestens 50 ms; nicht verfügbare Sensormesswerte bleiben NaN. Schnelle Signale benötigen eine unabhängig geprüfte Bandbreite und einen Anti-Aliasing-Filter.</string>
<string original="Enter coefficients measured on this apparatus. Defaults are nominal, not a calibration. Changing a coefficient recalculates the entire trace; original readings and settings are exported separately. Clearing data restores the defaults.">Am eigenen Aufbau gemessene Koeffizienten eingeben. Vorgaben sind Nennwerte, keine Kalibrierung. Änderungen berechnen die gesamte Kurve neu; ursprüngliche Messwerte und Einstellungen werden getrennt exportiert. Daten löschen setzt die Vorgaben zurück.</string>
        </translation>
    </translations>
    <data-containers>
	    <xi:include href="includes/containers_ch0_ch5.xml" xpointer="xpointer(/containers/node())" />
	    <!-- container for normalization to mV -->
	    <container size="0" static="false" init="">CH2_norm</container>
	    <container size="0" static="false" init="">CH3_norm</container>
	    <container size="0" static="false" init="">CH4_norm</container>
    <container size="1" init="3.225806451612903">gain_A0</container>
<container size="1" init="0">offset_A0</container>
<container size="1" init="3.225806451612903">gain_A1</container>
<container size="1" init="0">offset_A1</container>
<container size="1" init="3.225806451612903">gain_A2</container>
<container size="1" init="0">offset_A2</container>
    </data-containers>
    <input>
        <bluetooth mode="notification" rate="1" subscribeOnStart="false" id="Sense">
            <xi:include href="includes/bluetooth_outputs_ch1_ch5.xml" xpointer="xpointer(/outputs/node())" />
        </bluetooth>
    </input>
    <output>
        <bluetooth id="Sense">
            <config char="cddf1003-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" conversion="float32LittleEndian">9.0</config>
        </bluetooth>
    </output>
    <views>
        
        <view label="Graph">
            <graph label="Voltage at A0" aspectRatio="2.5" style="lines" lineWidth="1" color="green" partialUpdate="false" labelX="t" labelY="U" labelZ="" unitX="s" unitY="mV" unitZ="" logX="false" logY="false" logZ="false" xPrecision="3" yPrecision="3" zPrecision="3" scaleMinX="auto" scaleMaxX="auto" scaleMinY="auto" scaleMaxY="auto" scaleMinZ="auto" scaleMaxZ="auto" minX="0" maxX="0" minY="0" maxY="0" minZ="0" maxZ="0" mapWidth="0">
                <input axis="x">CH1</input>
                <input axis="y">CH2_norm</input>
            </graph>
            <graph label="Voltage at A1" aspectRatio="2.5" style="lines" lineWidth="1" color="blue" partialUpdate="false" labelX="t" labelY="U" labelZ="" unitX="s" unitY="mV" unitZ="" logX="false" logY="false" logZ="false" xPrecision="3" yPrecision="3" zPrecision="3" scaleMinX="auto" scaleMaxX="auto" scaleMinY="auto" scaleMaxY="auto" scaleMinZ="auto" scaleMaxZ="auto" minX="0" maxX="0" minY="0" maxY="0" minZ="0" maxZ="0" mapWidth="0">
                <input axis="x">CH1</input>
                <input axis="y">CH3_norm</input>
            </graph>
            <graph label="Voltage at A2" aspectRatio="2.5" style="lines" lineWidth="1" color="yellow" partialUpdate="false" labelX="t" labelY="U" labelZ="" unitX="s" unitY="mV" unitZ="" logX="false" logY="false" logZ="false" xPrecision="3" yPrecision="3" zPrecision="3" scaleMinX="auto" scaleMaxX="auto" scaleMinY="auto" scaleMaxY="auto" scaleMinZ="auto" scaleMaxZ="auto" minX="0" maxX="0" minY="0" maxY="0" minZ="0" maxZ="0" mapWidth="0">
                <input axis="x">CH1</input>
                <input axis="y">CH4_norm</input>
            </graph>
        </view>
        
        <view label="Simple">
            <value label="Voltage at A0" size="2" precision="3" unit="mV" color="green">
                <input>CH2_norm</input>
            </value>
            <value label="Voltage at A1" size="2" precision="3" unit="mV" color="blue">
                <input>CH3_norm</input>
            </value>
            <value label="Voltage at A2" size="2" precision="3" unit="mV" color="yellow">
                <input>CH4_norm</input>
            </value>
        </view>
        
        <!-- original view of raw sensor data: about 3.3mV per unit -->
        <view label="Raw Data">
            <graph label="Analog Input A0" aspectRatio="2.5" style="lines" lineWidth="1" color="ff7e22" partialUpdate="false" labelX="t" labelY="U" labelZ="" unitX="s" unitY="" unitZ="" logX="false" logY="false" logZ="false" xPrecision="3" yPrecision="3" zPrecision="3" scaleMinX="auto" scaleMaxX="auto" scaleMinY="auto" scaleMaxY="auto" scaleMinZ="auto" scaleMaxZ="auto" minX="0" maxX="0" minY="0" maxY="0" minZ="0" maxZ="0" mapWidth="0">
                <input axis="x">CH1</input>
                <input axis="y">CH2</input>
            </graph>
            <graph label="Analog Input A1" aspectRatio="2.5" style="lines" lineWidth="1" color="ff7e22" partialUpdate="false" labelX="t" labelY="U" labelZ="" unitX="s" unitY="" unitZ="" logX="false" logY="false" logZ="false" xPrecision="3" yPrecision="3" zPrecision="3" scaleMinX="auto" scaleMaxX="auto" scaleMinY="auto" scaleMaxY="auto" scaleMinZ="auto" scaleMaxZ="auto" minX="0" maxX="0" minY="0" maxY="0" minZ="0" maxZ="0" mapWidth="0">
                <input axis="x">CH1</input>
                <input axis="y">CH3</input>
            </graph>
            <graph label="Analog Input A2" aspectRatio="2.5" style="lines" lineWidth="1" color="ff7e22" partialUpdate="false" labelX="t" labelY="U" labelZ="" unitX="s" unitY="" unitZ="" logX="false" logY="false" logZ="false" xPrecision="3" yPrecision="3" zPrecision="3" scaleMinX="auto" scaleMaxX="auto" scaleMinY="auto" scaleMaxY="auto" scaleMinZ="auto" scaleMaxZ="auto" minX="0" maxX="0" minY="0" maxY="0" minZ="0" maxZ="0" mapWidth="0">
                <input axis="x">CH1</input>
                <input axis="y">CH4</input>
            </graph>
        </view>
    <view label="Setup">
    <info label="Use a common ground, short leads and inputs within 0–3.3 V; do not connect mains or negative voltages. Check the terminal voltage with a calibrated meter at two or more levels. Fit U=kq+c for each input, recording source resistance and meter loading. The default 3300/1023 mV/count is a nominal endpoint scale, not a measured ADC reference. High source impedance, sequential channel acquisition and RC loading can alter the result. Use slow signals or an appropriate anti-alias filter." />
    <info label="Record a stable reference before and after each trial. The BLE interval is at least 50 ms; unavailable sensor readings remain NaN. Fast signals need an independently verified bandwidth and anti-alias filtering." />
</view>
    <view label="Calibration">
    <info label="Enter coefficients measured on this apparatus. Defaults are nominal, not a calibration. Changing a coefficient recalculates the entire trace; original readings and settings are exported separately. Clearing data restores the defaults." />
    <edit label="Gain A0" unit="mV/count" default="3.225806451612903" decimal="true" signed="false" min="0.000000001">
        <output>gain_A0</output>
    </edit>
    <edit label="Offset A0" unit="mV" default="0" decimal="true" signed="true">
        <output>offset_A0</output>
    </edit>
    <edit label="Gain A1" unit="mV/count" default="3.225806451612903" decimal="true" signed="false" min="0.000000001">
        <output>gain_A1</output>
    </edit>
    <edit label="Offset A1" unit="mV" default="0" decimal="true" signed="true">
        <output>offset_A1</output>
    </edit>
    <edit label="Gain A2" unit="mV/count" default="3.225806451612903" decimal="true" signed="false" min="0.000000001">
        <output>gain_A2</output>
    </edit>
    <edit label="Offset A2" unit="mV" default="0" decimal="true" signed="true">
        <output>offset_A2</output>
    </edit>
</view>
    </views>
    
    <!-- Affine calibration U=kq+c; nominal endpoint scale is 3300/1023 mV/count. -->
    <analysis sleep="0.05">
    <formula formula="[1_]*[2]+[3]">
        <input clear="false">CH2</input>
        <input clear="false">gain_A0</input>
        <input clear="false">offset_A0</input>
        <output clear="true">CH2_norm</output>
    </formula>
    <formula formula="[1_]*[2]+[3]">
        <input clear="false">CH3</input>
        <input clear="false">gain_A1</input>
        <input clear="false">offset_A1</input>
        <output clear="true">CH3_norm</output>
    </formula>
    <formula formula="[1_]*[2]+[3]">
        <input clear="false">CH4</input>
        <input clear="false">gain_A2</input>
        <input clear="false">offset_A2</input>
        <output clear="true">CH4_norm</output>
    </formula>
</analysis>
    <export>
    <set name="Calibrated data (mV)">
            <data name="Time t (s)">CH1</data>
            <data name="Voltage at A0 (mV)">CH2_norm</data>
            <data name="Voltage at A1 (mV)">CH3_norm</data>
            <data name="Voltage at A2 (mV)">CH4_norm</data>
        </set>
        <set name="Raw data (ADC readings)">
            <data name="Time t (s)">CH1</data>
            <data name="Analog Input A0">CH2</data>
            <data name="Analog Input A1">CH3</data>
            <data name="Analog Input A2">CH4</data>
        </set>
    <set name="Calibration settings">
    <data name="Gain A0 (mV/count)">gain_A0</data>
    <data name="Offset A0 (mV)">offset_A0</data>
    <data name="Gain A1 (mV/count)">gain_A1</data>
    <data name="Offset A1 (mV)">offset_A1</data>
    <data name="Gain A2 (mV/count)">gain_A2</data>
    <data name="Offset A2 (mV)">offset_A2</data>
</set>
    <set name="Timing">
    <data name="Device time (s)">CH1</data>
    <data name="BLE receive time (s)">CH0</data>
</set>
    </export>
</phyphox>
